> git log --oneline
> git rebase -i HEAD~9


This will open the text editor, we'll see a list of commits alongside a list
of commands that we can choose from.
1. pick - use the commit
2. reword - use the commit, but edit the commit message
3. edit - use commit, but stop for amending
4. fixup - use commit content but meld it into previous commit and discard the commit
5. drop - remove commit